// std.crypto.legacy — Deprecated cryptographic algorithms for legacy interoperability only.
//
// WARNING: The algorithms in this module (such as MD5) are cryptographically broken
// and MUST NOT be used for security-sensitive contexts (e.g. password storage, digital
// signatures, HMAC authentication, or security tokens). They are provided strictly for
// backwards compatibility and interoperability with legacy protocols, legacy file checksums,
// and existing external data formats.
use "md5.vl"
